---
import SealedSection from '../seal/SealedSection.astro';
import SectionHead from '../ui/SectionHead.astro';
import SubHead from '../ui/SubHead.astro';
import Limits from '../ui/Limits.astro';

const docBase = 'https://github.com/Vulnetix/belai/blob/main/docs/';

const sealText =
  'Web sessions: while the Vulnetix CLI is logged in, every Belai session mirrors to the Vulnetix website. Belai → Sessions follows a running session live and takes prompts that run on the host as if typed there. When the host stops to ask, the page shows the question and can answer it: a permission ask (allow once, allow always, deny), clarify questions, the mode choice and a plan review. Tool rows, diffs with syntax colour, reasoning and every role-manager and classifier decision show as the TUI draws them. The session JSONL is the single record; the website mirrors it, and a web answer is untrusted input applied through the host\'s own code. The first answer wins. Belai → History also shows an audit trail of hosts and agents: facts Belai recorded about claims, commits, gates, pull requests and VEX, chained by SHA-256 so an edited row shows as broken.';

const answers = [
  {
    kind: 'permission',
    choices: 'allow once · allow always · deny',
    detail: 'The page shows the tool, its subject, the diff it would make and the exact rule allow-always adds. Allow-always writes that rule to the settings on the host, the same as pressing it there.',
  },
  {
    kind: 'question',
    choices: 'single or multiple choice · notes · skip · decline',
    detail: 'The questions the model asked, with every option and its description. Your answers still pass the prompt classifier on the host, like typed ones.',
  },
  {
    kind: 'mode',
    choices: 'the options on the mode panel',
    detail: 'When a request reads like a different mode than the one you set, the host asks before switching. Answer it from the page.',
  },
  {
    kind: 'plan review',
    choices: 'approve here · approve in a new session · refine · keep planning',
    detail: 'Read the plan on the page and approve it, or send notes back. Notes take the web-prompt path, so they are never a slash or shell command.',
  },
];

const records = [
  ['turn_state', 'a turn started or ended, with the footer facts: mode, model, effort, branch, switches, context'],
  ['tool_start', 'a tool call started, so the page shows it running before its result lands'],
  ['tool · diff', 'what a tool changed on disk, as the rows the TUI drew'],
  ['ask', 'the question the host is waiting on, keyed by its ask id'],
  ['ask_answer', 'how it was resolved, and whether the host or the web answered'],
  ['rolemanager', 'every classifier and role-manager verdict, with its label, model and timing'],
];

const path = [
  ['host', 'writes the line to the session JSONL'],
  ['syncer', 'uploads it about 30 ms later with the lines that came with it, gzipped when large'],
  ['server', 'Postgres notifications wake the page and the host inbox'],
  ['page', 'shows it, about one round trip after it happened'],
];

const audit = [
  ['host.first_seen · version_changed', 'this machine reported for the first time, or with a new Belai version'],
  ['host.rc_online · rc_offline', 'belai rc started or stopped'],
  ['host.dispatch', 'a request from the website (start, stop, worker, crew, pause, resume) and whether the host carried it out'],
  ['card.claimed · released', 'a worker took a card and handed it back, with the list it went to'],
  ['card.lease_lapsed', 'a claim ran out of lease and the card went back to its list'],
  ['repo.commit', 'the commit id Belai read from git, the base the branch started at and how many files changed'],
  ['gate.verified', 'a gate and the exit code that decided it, or a regression against the base'],
  ['vex.written · finding.carded', 'the VEX for a verdict, and the card a scan filed for a finding'],
];

const limits = [
  ['Only the open question', 'The host applies an answer only to the question open right now, and only if it fits: options that exist, one choice where only one is allowed, a known decision.'],
  ['Through the same code', "An answer is applied through the functions the host's own keys call. Notes are cleaned of control characters and capped."],
  ['First answer wins', 'If you answer at the terminal first, the page shows that the host refused the late one and why.'],
  ['Stays on the host', 'The agent picker and the first-run trust prompt are never answered from the web.'],
  ['Your switches', '`sync.remote_answers` turns web answers off and `sync.remote_prompts` makes a session view-only. A repository can switch either off; switching them on belongs to your own settings.'],
  ['The file is the record', 'Belai writes everything to the session JSONL first. The website mirrors those lines and never composes one.'],
];
---

<SealedSection label="web" sealText={sealText} id="web">
  <SectionHead title="Web sessions">
    While the Vulnetix CLI is logged in, each session mirrors to the Vulnetix website.{' '}
    <strong>Belai → Sessions</strong> follows a running session live, and a prompt you type there runs on
    the host as if you had typed it at the terminal.
  </SectionHead>

  <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
    <div class="mono min-w-0 rounded-xl border border-vx-ink p-5 text-xs leading-relaxed text-vx-ink/80 md:text-sm lg:col-span-7" aria-label="A permission ask as the Sessions page shows it" role="img">
      <p><span class="text-[#B86E00]">── permission</span> <span class="text-vx-ink/50">Edit · waiting for an answer ──</span></p>
      <p class="mt-3 pl-4"><span class="text-[#B86E00]">⌁</span> <span class="font-semibold text-vx-ink">Edit</span> internal/server/handler.go</p>
      <p class="pl-4 text-vx-ink/55">allow always adds Edit(internal/server/handler.go)</p>
      <div class="ml-4 mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg bg-vx-ink/5 py-1">
        <p class="whitespace-pre px-3"><span class="text-vx-ink/50"> 41</span>   ctx := r.Context()</p>
        <p class="whitespace-pre bg-vx-coral/15 px-3"><span class="text-[#B8332E]">−42</span>   user := r.URL.Query().Get("user")</p>
        <p class="whitespace-pre bg-vx-mint/25 px-3"><span class="text-vx-mint-strong">+42</span>   name := r.URL.Query().Get("user")</p>
        <p class="whitespace-pre bg-vx-mint/25 px-3"><span class="text-vx-mint-strong">+43</span>   if name == "" {'{'}</p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2 pl-4">
        <span class="rounded-md border border-vx-mint-strong px-3 py-1 text-vx-mint-strong">Allow once</span>
        <span class="rounded-md border border-vx-ink/30 px-3 py-1">Allow always</span>
        <span class="rounded-md border border-vx-ink/30 px-3 py-1 text-[#B8332E]">Deny</span>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="min-w-0 lg:col-span-5">
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold">Drawn like the TUI</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-vx-ink/80">
        The page draws with the TUI's own design system: thread blocks with a top rule, quiet tool rows that
        only turn red when they fail, reasoning folded to one line, diffs with line numbers and syntax colour,
        the plan with <span class="mono">◆ ◇ ✓</span>, and the footer's mode, model, switches and context
        gauge. Amber still means the host needs you. Open questions are also pinned above the composer, so
        you can find them in a long transcript.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-vx-ink/80">
        Classifier and role-manager decisions appear in the transcript as they happen: what was checked, the
        verdict, the model that gave it and how long it took. Switch on <span class="mono">all decisions</span>{' '}
        to also see the ones the TUI folds into its own lines, like mode selection and goal evaluation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <SubHead title="What you can answer from the web">
    When the host stops to ask you something, the page shows the question and you can answer it there.
    The host carries on as if you had pressed the key.
  </SubHead>
  <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-4">
    {answers.map((a, i) => (
      <article class={`flex flex-col rounded-xl border border-vx-ink p-5 ${i === 3 ? 'bg-vx-ink text-vx-cream' : ''}`}>
        <span class="h-1 w-10 rounded-full bg-vx-sand-amber"></span>
        <h4 class="mt-3 text-xl font-bold">{a.kind}</h4>
        <p class={`mono mt-1 text-xs ${i === 3 ? 'text-vx-mint' : 'text-vx-ink/60'}`}>{a.choices}</p>
        <p class={`mt-3 text-sm ${i === 3 ? 'text-vx-cream/80' : 'text-vx-ink/80'}`}>{a.detail}</p>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>

  <SubHead title="From the terminal to the page">
    The terminal never blocks on sync. Your answer travels the same way back to the host.
  </SubHead>
  <ol class="mt-8 grid list-none gap-3 p-0 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
    {path.map(([who, what], i) => (
      <li class={`relative rounded-xl border border-vx-ink p-5 ${i === 0 ? 'bg-vx-ink text-vx-cream' : ''}`}>
        <span class={`mono text-xs ${i === 0 ? 'text-vx-cream/60' : 'text-vx-ink/60'}`}>{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
        <p class={`mono mt-2 text-lg font-semibold ${i === 0 ? 'text-vx-mint' : ''}`}>{who}</p>
        <p class={`mt-1 text-sm ${i === 0 ? 'text-vx-cream/80' : 'text-vx-ink/75'}`}>{what}</p>
        {i < path.length - 1 && <span class="mono absolute -right-2.5 top-1/2 hidden -translate-y-1/2 text-vx-mint-strong lg:block" aria-hidden="true">▸</span>}
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <div class="mt-8 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="min-w-0 rounded-xl bg-vx-ink p-5 lg:col-span-7">
      <p class="mono text-xs tracking-wider text-vx-cream/70">WHAT THE SESSION FILE HOLDS</p>
      <dl class="mono mt-3 grid gap-x-4 gap-y-2 text-sm sm:grid-cols-[8rem_minmax(0,1fr)]">
        {records.map(([name, what]) => (
          <>
            <dt class="text-vx-mint">{name}</dt>
            <dd class="m-0 font-sans text-vx-cream/80">{what}</dd>
          </>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div class="min-w-0 lg:col-span-5">
      <p class="text-vx-ink/80">
        A resumed session reads the same lines, so the page and the terminal show the same events. Resume
        a session with <code class="mono">belai -r</code> and its diffs and answered questions are back on
        screen. History hides sessions run in <code class="mono">/tmp</code> until you ask for them.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        The website's Agent Builder uses a live session too. It sends the host a one-line premise, and the
        host checks it like a typed prompt, drafts an agent profile with its own model, and sends back each
        field with a reason. Nothing is saved on the host. The request needs web prompts on, runs one at a
        time per session, and expires after three minutes.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm">
        <a class="text-vx-ink underline" href={`${docBase}session-sync.md`}>docs/session-sync.md</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <SubHead title="An audit trail of hosts and agents" id="audit">
    Sync also carries a second record: what your hosts and agents did. <strong>Belai → History</strong> shows
    it in two tabs beside the session list.
  </SubHead>
  <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
    <article class="rounded-xl border border-vx-ink p-5">
      <span class="h-1 w-10 rounded-full bg-vx-sand-amber"></span>
      <h4 class="mt-3 text-xl font-bold">Hosts</h4>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-vx-ink/80">
        Each machine that runs Belai: when it was first seen, the Belai versions and hostnames it has run under,
        when remote control came online or went offline, and every request the website made of it with how the
        host answered. Open a host to read its own log, which follows new events as they arrive.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="rounded-xl border border-vx-ink bg-vx-ink p-5 text-vx-cream">
      <span class="h-1 w-10 rounded-full bg-vx-sand-amber"></span>
      <h4 class="mt-3 text-xl font-bold">Agents</h4>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-vx-cream/80">
        Every claim and release of a card, the commit an agent left on the item's branch, each gate decided by
        its exit code, the draft pull request and the VEX. A row about a vulnerability links to it, to the card
        and to the session that did the work. Filter by vulnerability, card, agent or repository.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-8 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="min-w-0 rounded-xl bg-vx-ink p-5 lg:col-span-7">
      <p class="mono text-xs tracking-wider text-vx-cream/70">WHAT THE AUDIT LOG HOLDS</p>
      <dl class="mono mt-3 grid gap-x-4 gap-y-2 text-sm sm:grid-cols-[13rem_minmax(0,1fr)]">
        {audit.map(([name, what]) => (
          <>
            <dt class="text-vx-mint">{name}</dt>
            <dd class="m-0 font-sans text-vx-cream/80">{what}</dd>
          </>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div class="min-w-0 lg:col-span-5">
      <p class="text-vx-ink/80">
        An event is a fixed set of identifiers: a worker profile, a card id, a branch, a commit id, an advisory
        id and an enum verdict. A prompt, a reply, a command, tool output or a file has no field to go in, and
        Belai stamps the time and the order itself.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        Each event carries the SHA-256 of itself and the event before it, so an edited or missing row breaks
        every hash after it. The Verify chain button on the page re-checks the stored rows and names the
        first event that no longer fits.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        The log travels with sync: <span class="mono">/sync off</span> stops it, a repository can switch sync
        off, and switching it on belongs to your own settings.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm">
        <a class="text-vx-ink underline" href={`${docBase}audit.md`}>docs/audit.md</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Limits items={limits} class="mt-16" />
</SealedSection>
